# Unanchored, not just `/target`: `cargo check -p <crate>`/`cargo kani`/
# `cross check` invocations from inside a crate's own directory (or with
# a scoped `--target-dir`) have left real per-crate `target/` build
# output at `crates/*/target/` alongside the shared workspace-root one --
# the same kind of throwaway artifact either way, just at a different
# path than the anchored pattern originally assumed.
target/

# Creusot: local why3find scratch state and crash reports; `verif/` (the
# proof cache) and `why3find.json` ARE tracked, matching elicitation's own
# convention — durable evidence a contract actually proved, not rebuilt
# from scratch every time.
.why3find/
rustc-ice-*.txt

# Verus: `verus --crate-type=lib` (invoked as a bare compiler, not through
# Cargo) drops its compiled rlib next to the source tree with no way to
# redirect it -- a throwaway build artifact, not evidence (unlike
# Creusot's verif/ .coma/proof.json files, which stay tracked). Unanchored
# (not just `/liblib.rlib` at the root) since the actual drop location has
# moved before and any stray rlib anywhere in the tree is the same kind of
# throwaway artifact; `just verify-verus` also deletes it once the run's
# outcome is printed, this is a backstop.
*.rlib
